<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Hægefjell from Landtakdammen — Landtakdammen–main Hægefjell dry snow-free return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the Landtakdammen parking area, use its existing walking access onto Borstadvegen, then follow the ordinary mountain paths to the main Hægefjell summit walking ground. Return to the same parking ingress by the exact same course. This recommendation is for the established hiking approach, not any climbing route, an extended loop or a visit to the mountain&apos;s slab margins.

Choose dry, snow-free conditions. Granite slabs can become very slippery when wet or icy; fog and poor visibility make the open upper terrain difficult to follow. Stay well back from slab margins and summit drops. Wear suitable footwear and carry map and compass, warm and waterproof clothing, food, drink and enough daylight. Turn back if weather, visibility, footing or navigation becomes uncertain. Confirm current road and parking access, local signs, trail conditions and lawful restrictions before departure; the whole itinerary is unavailable if a required leg is closed, prohibited or unsafe. Walk considerately on the established paths, avoid vegetation damage, wildlife disturbance, litter and shortcuts. No climbing or camping permission is implied.

Waymarking is partial: some mountain approach sections are mapped as marked, while continuous marking on the upper footpath and summit approach is not confirmed. Do not rely on the map or markings alone. The source is descriptive community mapping, not a current field survey or a guarantee of safe or open ground.

The complete mapped return is approximately 8.8 km. The inherited 750 m ascent, 750 m descent and 330 minutes remain approximate legacy planning estimates, not surveyed heights, a measured elevation profile or a time guarantee. No elevations are assigned, and no height estimate is copied from the generated Komoot route.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. Open Database License 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. Whole original source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=8.35,59.25,8.42,59.285. Changes: original source road/path vertices ordered at literal shared nodes from the actual parking ingress to the main walking summit terminal, then exactly reversed to return; canonical display simplified with the existing source-vertex helper. No coordinate snapping, peak-point replacement, synthetic connectors, private operator-track donation or elevation assignment. Descriptive planning geometry; not navigation-grade.

